 lorehead:"FROM THE EPIC",
 loreok:"Continue ▸",
 lore0:"\"Qırq qız\" (Forty Maidens) is the heroic epic of the Karakalpak people, sung for centuries by bards with the qobız fiddle.\n\nIn the city of Sarkop lived the brave Allayar Bay. He had six sons and a daughter, Gulayim. At fourteen she asked her father for the land of Miywali, built a fortress there and trained forty maidens with sword and bow.\n\nOne dawn the Kalmyk khan Surtaysha fell upon Sarkop with forty thousand riders…",
 lore1:"During the raid Gulayim and her maidens were training in the Qiran mountains. She returned to find Sarkop in ashes, her father and six brothers dead and her people driven off in chains.\n\nGulayim swears to avenge her father and free her people.",
 lore2:"In the epic some young men of Sarkop bowed to Surtaysha out of fear. Gulayim knew fear from betrayal — in this chapter she meets one of them.",
 lore3:"Sarkop's hero Otbasqan never bowed, even in captivity: Surtaysha tormented him and loaded him with two sacks, yet he never begged. In this chapter Gulayim sets him free.",
 lore4:"Gulayim and her maidens ride along the Astrakhan sea, raiding Kalmyk caravans. In the game the captives are to be shipped away, guarded by a sea dragon.",
 lore5:"An ambush waits in the Derbent mountains. The Kalmyk champion Qunqar, called a \"dev\" in the epic, kills Otbasqan. Sarbinaz fights him for three days and wins on the fourth. You play this chapter as Sarbinaz.",
 lore6:"Most captives are held in the city of Qashal. Its king Qargashiq stands six arshins tall, dark-faced with a white moustache and a golden helmet, riding a black horse.",
 lore7:"The epic's most famous scene is the duel of Gulayim and Surtaysha: their swords bend like sickles, so they wrestle bound by a double chain, day and night. Allayar's arrow never pierced Surtaysha's golden helmet — now his magic must be broken with the powers gathered on the way.",
 use6:"Earth Slam (1) stuns chained, armoured foes. You will need it against the executioner.",
 use7:"The Chain (2) pulls an enemy to you — even a sea monster onto the shore.",
 use8:"Water Shield (▼) blocks fire and blood magic. Qunqar's fire cannot pass it.",
 use9:"Dev Strength (▼) makes you a giant for a while — enough to face Qargashiq.",
 use0:"The Black Rider (▼) breaks through enemy lines.",
 x2a:"Sand hides tracks, but caravan wheels cut deep. We are close.",
 x2b:"Every step is for my father's blood. Maidens, hold the line!",
 x3a:"Smoke by the river. The caravan has stopped.",
 x3b:"Captives first, then the executioner. Otbasqan must be there.",
 x4a:"The sea… We never saw the sea in Sarkop.",
 x4b:"Not even the sea will stop us!",
 x5a:"Gulayim, I couldn't save Otbasqan… Now I will avenge him. Follow me!",
 x6a:"Hundreds of Sarkop's people are locked behind Qashal's gate.",
 x6b:"No gate is thicker than the will of forty maidens.",
 x7a:"Here is Surtaysha's horde. My father never made it here.",
 x7b:"We made it, Gulayim. Forty maidens follow you.",
 x7c:"Today Sarkop takes back what is hers!",
