 nar6:"The captive caravan was driven east across the salt flats. Gulayim and her forty maidens followed the trail.",
 nar7:"By the river the caravan halted. Among the chained captives was Otbasqan, hero of Sarkop.",
 nar8:"The Kalmyks meant to load the captives onto ships and carry them across the sea.",
 nar9:"An ambush waited in the Derbent mountains. Qunqar the dev struck Otbasqan down. Avenging him falls to Sarbinaz.",
 nar10:"Most of the captives were locked inside the city of Qashal, ruled by Qargashiq, six arshins tall.",
 nar11:"The road ended at Surtaysha's horde. Blood totems, black magic and the last of the captives…",
 nar12:"Surtaysha fell. His black magic faded, and the monster-soldiers became men again.",
 nar13:"The freed people returned to Sarkop. Sarbinaz carved the names of the fallen in gold upon stone. At her father's grave Gulayim whispered: \"I have avenged you, father.\"",
